The diagrams show the readings before and after object P is fully submerged. Object Q displaces $86$ mL. Neither measurement spills water. Which object has the greater volume, and how much more water does it displace?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\definecolor{waterBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw (0,3)--(0,0)--(2,0)--(2,3);
\draw (4,3)--(4,0)--(6,0)--(6,3);
\draw[waterBlue] (0,1.5)--(2,1.5);
\draw[waterBlue] (4,1.735)--(6,1.735);
\draw (4.65,0.35)--(5.2,0.3)--(5.4,0.65)--(5.1,1.05)--(4.7,0.85)--cycle;
\path (1,1.5) node[above] {$0.600\text{ L}$};
\path (5,1.735) node[above] {$0.694\text{ L}$};
\path (1,0) node[below] {Before P};
\path (5,0) node[below] {After P};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
